I've created a new version of my Hobbit patch that fixes a few bugs
that were in previous versions:

 * Fixed problem with Hobbits changing to size medium when changing
back from
a polymorphed state
 * Hobbits now shrink out of most body armors when changing back into
Hobbit
form
 * Non caveman and non-tourist Hobbits are now generated either with a
cream pie
or pancake (instead of just the former)

I'd like to thank Sam Dennis for helping me to navigate the code well
enough to fix the size-changing bug.

This will likely be the last version of the patch I release for a
while, barring any other bug-fixes that are needed.

Now my question is: does anyone use this patch?  Is it worth
submitting to the devteam (not that they accept very many patches)?

Anyway, the patch, along with a description of what it does, and a
Windows "reference binary" is available at:

http://www.homebrew.net/~karlos/


